4,"playId":"401862786264","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7368,"playId":"401862786269","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7509,"playId":"401862786273","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7277,"playId":"401862786276","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.737,"playId":"401862786281","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7388,"playId":"401862786286","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.6955,"playId":"401862786290","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.6592,"playId":"401862786294","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.6689,"playId":"401862786299","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.6949,"playId":"401862786302","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7128,"playId":"401862786306","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7654,"playId":"401862786311","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7475,"playId":"401862786316","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7477,"playId":"401862786321","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7297,"playId":"401862786324","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7242,"playId":"401862786327","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7328,"playId":"401862786331","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7388,"playId":"401862786334","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7116,"playId":"401862786338","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.7101,"playId":"401862786343","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.6801,"playId":"401862786347","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3674","guid":"26aa1b95-3732-3b7c-bbe7-d784905b178b","fullName":"H. A. Chapman Stadium","address":{"city":"Tulsa","state":"OK","zipCode":"74104","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/interior/3674.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day","interior"]}]},"attendance":14938},"article":{"headline":"Tayven Jackson throws 4 TD passes, runs for TD in OT as UNT beats Tulsa 45-44","description":"— Tayven Jackson threw a season-high four touchdown passes and added a 1-yard rushing TD in overtime, Jahiem White had 219 yards rushing and a touchdown, and North Texas beat Tulsa 45-44 on Thursday night in the American Conference opener for both teams.","story":"TULSA, Okla. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4801307/tayven-jackson\" target=\"_new\">Tayven Jackson</a> threw a season-high four touchdown passes and added a 1-yard rushing TD in overtime, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4911971/jahiem-white\" target=\"_new\">Jahiem White</a> had 219 yards rushing and a touchdown, and North Texas beat Tulsa 45-44 on Thursday night in the American Conference opener for both teams. \n\n\r\n              Jackson was 24-of-39 passing for 332 yards with two interceptions. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4827049/max-reese\" target=\"_new\">Max Reese</a> had five receptions for 101 yards and a touchdown and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5122082/justin-stevenson\" target=\"_new\">Justin Stevenson</a> had two TD receptions for the Mean Green (3-2). \n\n\r\n              Jackson hit <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5085503/grayson-o'bara\" target=\"_new\">Grayson O'Bara</a> for a 22-yard gain on the first play of overtime and scored on a short run three plays later. \n\n\r\n              Tulsa's <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4685699/damari-alston\" target=\"_new\">Damari Alston</a> ran for a 2-yard touchdown on the second possession of OT, but the 2-point conversion attempt was short. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5224011/baylor-hayes\" target=\"_new\">Baylor Hayes</a> threw three touchdown passes and ran for two more scores for the Golden Hurricane (3-2). \n\n\r\n              Jackson found Koch for a 39-yard gain before White scored on a 14-yard run that made it a two-touchdown game with 6:13 remaining in the third. \n\n\r\n              White has 10 total touchdowns (eight rushing, two receiving) this season, second most in the Football Bowl Subdivision behind <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079322/jadan-baugh\" target=\"_new\">Jadan Baugh</a>'s 11 for Florida. \n\n\r\n              Hayes hit <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5157287/david-wells-jr\" target=\"_new\">David Wells Jr</a>. for touchdown passes of 5 yards late in the third and 4 yards with 8:17 left in the game to make it 31-all. \n\n\r\n              After Jackson connected with Stevenson for 14-yard touchdown that put UNT back in front, Hayes scored on a 1-yard run with 31 seconds left in regulation to force overtime. \n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next </hl2>\r\n              North Texas: Hosts Charlotte on Oct. 10. \n\n\r\n              Tulsa: Plays Oct. 10 at Navy. \n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>, visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-02T05:36:38Z"}}